  :notes
    "LLM auto-approve proposal v0 is the third autonomy knob layered over the wave-15 / 16 review-resolution surface. The first knob — wave-18 / task 07 review_automation_policy (manual | suggest | auto_safe) — runs a deterministic safety inspector and MAY auto-promote to Approved when every rule passes. The second knob — wave-20 / task 08 auto_answer_policy (off | deterministic_safe | dry_run) — plumbs the same deterministic inspector into the LISTENER path. This third knob — auto_approve_mode (off | sonnet_suggest) — asks Sonnet to PROPOSE a structured review decision and surfaces it for operator review WITHOUT ever applying it in v0. The three knobs are ORTHOGONAL and CO-EXIST on the response when supplied; the proposal NEVER overrides the deterministic policy outcome and the deterministic policy NEVER overrides an explicit caller `review_decision`. Strict invariants (pinned by 22 new pure tests + the enforce_proposal_invariants helper): (I1) NEVER auto-reject — the parser collapses any model-side `rejected` to `needs_changes` with a `proposal_warnings[]` entry; the wire NEVER carries decision=rejected. (I2) Destructive actions (archive | supersede | remove, case-insensitive) ALWAYS short-circuit to `destructive_blocked` BEFORE the Sonnet call — proposal=None on the bundle, requires_human=true forced; the audit row carries a loud `rule:destructive_action` warning. (I3) `applied=false` pinned on EVERY proposal regardless of confidence; `requires_human=true` forced even on non-destructive actions in v0 (propose-only). Any future wave that wants to promote a proposal to authority MUST add a separate explicit caller-side opt-in flag — this knob ONLY ever proposes. (I4) Sonnet unavailable surfaces `LlmAutoApproveProposalStatus::Unavailable` with a non-empty `unavailable_reason` and zero proposals. NO fallback to a deterministic suggestion (mirrors `feedback_fail_fast_no_fallback`); NO silent success. (I5) `destructive_check` is ALWAYS overwritten with the deterministic `is_destructive_review_action` outcome via enforce_proposal_invariants, regardless of what the model replied; the model's value lands in `proposal_warnings[]` for audit but never on the wire. Strict-enum parsing: typo `auto_approve_mode=\"auto\"` fails fast with INVALID_PARAM (parse_proposer_mode_or_error / parse_plan_proposer_mode_or_error) BEFORE any DB read so caller typos never silently degrade to off. Wire shape (stamp_llm_auto_approve_proposal_payload): {llm_auto_approve_proposal_mode, llm_auto_approve_proposal_status (not_invoked|llm_unavailable|suggested|destructive_blocked|no_suggestion), llm_auto_approve_proposal {decision, confidence, evidence, non_goal_check, destructive_check, requires_human, applied=false} (omitted under unavailable per invariant I4), llm_auto_approve_proposal_warnings[], llm_auto_approve_proposal_unavailable_reason (only under unavailable), llm_auto_approve_proposal_action, llm_auto_approve_proposal_caller, llm_auto_approve_proposal_model}. attach_directive_proposal_block / attach_plan_proposal_block skip the splice when status=NotInvoked so legacy callers (mode=off / mode absent) stay byte-identical with pre-wave-21. The Sonnet system prompt enumerates the six required JSON fields and the I1 (NEVER respond rejected) constraint; the user prompt carries the surface label, action, artifact id + version, the deterministic inspector summary (review_automation_policy + review_automation_status + explicit_decision_supplied), and an optional artifact digest (the directive's sexp_text or plan.sexp_text when available). Sonnet token budget capped at 1024 (proposals + short justification fit comfortably). Wired into 10 branch sites total: directive.action_approve (legacy / with_resolution / with_policy_only) + directive.action_archive (legacy / with_resolution / with_policy_only) + plan.action_approve (legacy / with_resolution / with_policy_only) + plan.action_mark (legacy / with_resolution / with_policy_only) + plan.action_supersede (legacy / with_resolution / with_policy_only). On every branch the proposer runs AFTER the existing wave-15/18/20 logic so the deterministic outcome is already on the payload when the proposer fires, and the proposer NEVER mutates the deterministic decision — both surfaces stay independent. Caller-supplied `review_decision` ALWAYS wins (the proposal is informational only); the deterministic `review_automation_policy` outcome (auto_safe / suggest / auto_safe_blocked) ALWAYS wins (the proposal does not override it). Co-existence design: dashboards can see all three knobs' outputs (review_automation_policy / auto_answer_policy / auto_approve_mode) on the same response and pivot on whichever signal they trust most. The MCP descriptors document the three knobs as ORTHOGONAL and pin the propose-only invariant. Acceptance: review_gate::tests 180/180 (+22 new); directive::tests 43/43; plan::tests 271/271; cargo test -p missiond-daemon 1420/1420 (+28 from 1392 baseline; six tests in other modules also incrementally count toward the 28 because the enforce_proposal_invariants helper is exercised via stamp tests + LlmAutoApproveProposalBundle constructors); cargo test -p missiond-mcp --lib 17/17; cargo build --workspace clean; check-architecture-lisp --all-v2 20 files; git diff --check no whitespace. cargo test -p missiond-core 327/327 (orthogonal — not touched). Pre-commit task-scope-guard --mode staged: 5 staged files, all in :write-scope (no out-of-scope leakage). Post-commit verify-task-contract.mjs: e14077383b09 against contract OK (commit message `feat(review): propose LLM auto approvals` matches contract; scope check write-scope-only OK; must-not-touch clean — workflow.rs / agent_execution.rs / workstation_dispatch.rs / plan_dag.rs / .missiond/v2/*.lisp / scripts/** all untouched). Report written out-of-scope to .missiond/tasks/wave21/reports/wave21-06-llm-auto-approve-proposal-v0.report.lisp; intentionally untracked per wave21 protocol. workflow.rs (wave21-07 scope) deliberately untouched — review-resolve workflow surface stays for the next task. Conservative boundary recap: default OFF (mode=off / field absent both preserve byte-shape); propose-only (applied=false / requires_human=true pinned per invariant I3); I1 NEVER auto-reject; I2 destructive NEVER auto-promoted (short-circuit BEFORE LLM call); I3 NO actual auto-approve in v0 (propose-only); I4 Sonnet unavailable surfaces llm_unavailable, NO deterministic fallback; I5 destructive_check ALWAYS deterministic, never model. Future-wave hook: any explicit promote-proposal-to-authority knob must be a NEW caller-side opt-in flag — this knob's contract is propose-only forever."
